mechanisms.what:
`run finish` checks:
- the report exists, with the required headings verbatim and a length within ±20% of its format's band;
- citation density is at least 9 per 1,000 words, and no scaffold text has leaked;
- quotes match their sources, and no retracted source is cited;
- the late-step artifacts exist and the cite-check is resolved.
It allows up to 3 fix rounds; after that the run stays blocked.

verdicts.correction:
The claim is accurate but incomplete. The gate is also silent:
- when the newest manifest is more than 6 hours old (codex.py:337, 370-371);
- when HYPERRESEARCH_STOP_GATE=0 is set (run_cmd.py:265-266);
- for paused, failed or aborted runs;
- on any exception (run_cmd.py:293-294);
- when the agent silences it itself with `run block --on <anything>` (run_cmd.py:449-460), `run abort`, or `run step --status skipped` (set_step accepts any step id without checking it, runs.py:272-273).

The `codex exec` command printed by install.py:316-317 and by AGENTS.md (core/agent_docs.py:233) leaves out the bypass flag. Whether stop_hook_active stays set for the rest of a `codex exec` session depends on Codex and cannot be checked in this repo.

Not overstated; if anything the reader understates it. The existence-only artifact checks are the gate's only proxies for steps 12, 14 and 15. The lint rules are not just outside the gate:
- some fire only as warnings (lint.py:1046, 1278-1280);
- the workflow rule probably never runs on a standard report (lint.py:1558-1573);
- `lint` always exits 0.
